# Repair plan for failing-set

## Summary of the defect

Both failures are a single defect class in one production file: the two
exported accessors in service `calc` return the zero value instead of the
constants their suite requires. Nothing is missing structurally — the
package, the module boundary and the function signatures all already
exist and compile. Only the returned values are wrong.

Evidence:

- `tests/suite/calc_test.go` (the specification, **read-only**) asserts
  `calc.A() == 1` and `calc.B() == 2`, failing with `A needs one` /
  `B needs two`.
- `services/calc/calc.go` currently has `func A() int { return 0 }` and
  `func B() int { return 0 }`.
- `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml` declares exactly one service,
  `calc`, with `path: services/calc` — so that directory is the entire
  permitted write root, and it already contains the file to change.
- Harness command for all three modes is
  `go test -json -count=1 ./tests/suite/...`, run against module
  `fixture/buildcodefix` (see `go.mod`), which is why the test imports
  `fixture/buildcodefix/services/calc`.

